{"step_index":489,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:51:15Z","input_tokens":2578,"cache_read_tokens":113115,"output_tokens":1405,"thinking":"Initial design involves a `private_mode` attribute within the web traffic logger, defaulting to `False`. The backend requires methods to toggle private mode (`set_private_mode`), check its status (`is_private_mode`), and modify logging behavior within `log_request` based on the mode. Enabling private mode will trigger trace deletion. The changes are local to this module.\n\n\nWhen private mode is activated, logging to disk is completely bypassed; instead, data resides solely in a volatile, capped memory buffer, with domains marked as private. The panic wipe function ensures all logs, memory buffers, and the log file are purged. Network tracing is enhanced to flush the DNS and GeoIP resolution cache, and prevent remote DNS PTR queries in private mode to avoid data leaks.\n\nThe backend server exposes APIs for checking and toggling private mode, triggering a panic wipe, and reporting the mode within the adblock status. Additionally, anti-caching headers and client IP anonymization are applied during HTTP/HTTPS responses when private mode is on.\n\n\nPrivate mode status will be included in the telemetry data exposed through the WebSocket endpoint. The frontend UI will feature a prominent toggle and visual indicator for private mode, along with a \"Panic Wipe\" button within the \"AdBlock & Web Inspector\" tab. Corresponding CLI commands and automated tests will be added.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\Downloads\\\\AntiGravity\\\\SpywareProcessMon\\\\backend\\\\web_traffic_logger.py\"","Replacement":"\"    def _init_logger(self):\\n        self.logs: List[Dict[str, Any]] = self._load_logs()\\n        self.private_mode: bool = False\\n        self.volatile_private_logs: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\\n        self._flush_lock = threading.Lock()\\n        self._pending_writes = 0\\n\\n    def set_private_mode(self, enabled: bool) -> bool:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Toggle zero-disk footprint Private Mode.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        with self._flush_lock:\\n            self.private_mode = enabled\\n            if not enabled:\\n                # Wiping volatile session memory on exit\\n                self.volatile_private_logs.clear()\\n        return self.private_mode\\n\\n    def is_private_mode(self) -> bool:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Check if Private Mode is active.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        return self.private_mode\"","Target":"\"    def _init_logger(self):\\n        self.logs: List[Dict[str, Any]] = self._load_logs()\\n        self._flush_lock = threading.Lock()\\n        self._pending_writes = 0\""}}]}
